DOOM1.WAD is not included in this repository.

It's id Software's copyrighted level/asset data, so it isn't redistributed
here — you provide your own copy locally and the build reads it from this
folder (`assets/DOOM1.WAD`, gitignored, never committed).

Two ways to get one:

1. The free shareware/demo WAD (recommended — this is what the project is
   built and tested against). It's freely distributable under id Software's
   own shareware terms. Search for "DOOM1.WAD shareware download" or grab it
   from any long-standing Doom archive (e.g. the id Software / Doom releases
   mirrored on archive.org).

2. Your own licensed copy of the full game (e.g. via Steam/GOG), if you want
   to point the pipeline at commercial IWAD data instead. Not required —
   the shareware WAD is sufficient for everything this project currently
   builds (E1M1).

Once you have it:

    cp /path/to/DOOM1.WAD assets/DOOM1.WAD
    python3 tools/wad2reu.py assets/DOOM1.WAD -o build/assets.reu

See tools/wad2reu.py --help for the full set of options.
